452	106,1056,340,1352	452. Flower of Virginia Waterleaf.	A Virginia Waterleaf flower: a small bell-shaped corolla with five long stamens standing far out of it, set in a narrow, hairy, five-parted calyx.
453	406,1076,763,1340	453. Corolla laid open, and stamens.	The Waterleaf corolla slit and spread open: a fan of five lobes with narrow bearded strips inside, and five long stamens radiating from its base.
454	835,1068,1148,1359	454. Calyx and young pod, with the style.	The calyx spread out in five narrow, bristly-fringed lobes around the round young pod, with the long style curling up from its top.
